--- !u!114 &7411072381853963737
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'The <b>Player Name Tag</b> prefab displays a UI indicator anchored above the Player Avatar''s head, which shows participants names and their microphone status.


      When a person speaks and their microphone is active, a subtle pulse effect is displayed to visualize sound emission. If a person does not have their microphone set to active, the microphone icon will update to indicate the microphone is currently muted.


      The <b>Player Name Tag (Script)</b> component also provides an LOD system, which controls the visual states of the Player Name Tag based on distance and gaze, this is helpful to manage visual noise when multiple people are gathered in a room.

'
